  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$What is the significance of positive versus negative values in the coordinates used to calculate distances between points A and M' after ΔADM has been reflected twice in different axes? Does it affect the final result? Explain. __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$No, because we only care about absolute value differences$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If a triangle's sides are calculated using x-coordinates (x1) and y-coordinates (y2), what does this imply about their orientation relative to each other in terms of distance calculation? Do the lengths change based on which axis is used for coordinates? Explain. __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$No, because we only care about absolute value differences$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$What do you observe when ΔADM is reflected in the x-axis and y-axis consecutively compared to its original position without any reflections? Are the lengths of sides AD, DM, and MA affected by these consecutive reflections? Explain briefly. __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$No; Because we only care about absolute value differences$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If ΔADM is reflected in both axes (x-axis first, then y-axis), what would be the new coordinates of A' after the initial reflection in the x-axis and subsequent reflection in the y-axis? What are they now compared to their original positions? __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$(−3, 1) and (−9, 6)$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$What is true about the angles in ΔA'M'D' compared to ΔADM after it has been reflected twice in different axes? Are these reflections symmetrical or asymmetrical? Explain. __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$Symmetrical; Because we only care about absolute value differences$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In Fig. 1.7, if x-coordinates of A and M are added to their y-coordinate counterparts, what do you get for each calculation? Are these calculations the same or different in terms of values obtained? ___________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$(3 + 9) = 12 and (4 + 6) = 10$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$What does the final result of AD, when ΔADM is reflected twice consecutively in different axes (x-axis first, then y-axis), indicate about the triangle's orientation relative to its original position? Does it affect the length of side AD? Explain. __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$No; Because we only care about absolute value differences$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If ΔADM is reflected in both x and y axes consecutively, what can be concluded about the final lengths of sides AD, DM, MA after these reflections? Do they remain unchanged or change based on how coordinates are used for each reflection? Explain. __________$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$No; Because we only care about absolute value differences$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The distance between points _______ and D' is calculated using the Baudhāyana–Pythagoras Theorem.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$C and C'D'$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For point W with x-coordinate -5, if it lies on a line parallel to the y-axis, its coordinates would be (_______, –6).$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$(−5, –6) or (5, –6) depending on Quadrant$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If points R, A, M, and P form a quadrilateral where PA is perpendicular to RM, which axis must M lie on for these sides to be perpendicular? _______ axis.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$x-axis$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Given the right-angled triangle IZN with Z at (5, -6), calculate side IN if its hypotenuse NZ measures 10 units. The length of side IN is _______ units.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$8$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Given the triangle with vertices A (3, –4), B (–2, 6), and C (7, 10), what is the length of side AB when calculated using the distance formula? The answer will be in terms of _______ units.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$√53$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For the points R (-5, -1), B (-2, -5), C (4, -12), determine whether these lie on the same straight line. If so, prove your answer using two distinct methods: algebraic and graphical. (_______) is one such method.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$Algebraic$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Using a right-angled triangle IZN where Z has coordinates (5, -6) and N has coordinates (10, -6), find the length of side IN using the distance formula. The answer should be in terms of √29 units.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$√29$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For point M(–7, 1) as midpoint of A(3, –4) and B(x, y), solve for x and y to locate points A and B correctly. (_______ , _______ ).$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$(−10, −2)$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In the context of triangle ABC with midpoints D(5, 1), E(6, 5), F(0, 3) found, what are the coordinates of vertex A? Assuming all calculations and methods are correct, the answer should be in terms of √10 units.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$(2, -4)$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true);
INSERT INTO public.question_bank (institution_id, subject_id, topic_id, grade_level_id, class_group_id, question_text, question_type, options, correct_answer, marks, difficulty_level, tags, source, created_by, is_approved) VALUES
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The use of coordinates is a relatively recent concept compared to its usage in navigation and ancient geometry.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Baudhāyana used East–West and North–South lines for his geometric constructions, laying foundational work that later influenced Descartes' coordinate system.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Āryabhaṭa introduced the concept of zero as an algebraic entity in his work on celestial coordinates.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The introduction of negative numbers by Brahmagupta was crucial for developing the modern four-quadrant Cartesian plane, a cornerstone of coordinate geometry.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The Indian decimal system and algebraic formalism significantly influenced Omar Khayyam's approach to solving geometric problems using coordinates in the plane.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Brahmagupta’s work on negative numbers was foundational for what Descartes would later build upon when he developed the coordinate system.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The Greek mathematician Ptolemy used Indian trigonometric methods to calculate longitudes and latitudes of cities, influencing his geographical works.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Coordinates were first introduced on Earth's surface by Ujjayinī as a reference for measuring other locations around the world.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Baudhāyana’s work laid the groundwork for the Baudhāyana–Pythagoras Theorem, which is central to modern coordinate geometry.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Al-Bīrūnī's travels and studies in India contributed to his development of the astrolabe, a tool used by sailors to find their coordinates using celestial navigation.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The Ujjayinī meridian as a zero-longitude reference for early Arabic maps was not influenced by Indian mathematical works but rather from Greek traditions.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Al-Bīrūnī's work with the astrolabe and his studies in India combined to form a complete navigational system that allowed sailors precise coordinate calculations.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Omar Khayyam mathematicians' approach of interpreting algebraic problems geometrically using coordinates was unique and did not follow earlier Indian works.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The concept of negative numbers was introduced by Aryabhata, which was later refined by Brahmagupta to create the zero-centric coordinate plane we study today.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The grid-based thinking used in ancient urban planning is a direct precursor to modern Cartesian coordinates and their use in navigation.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Descartes' formalisation of coordinates as two numbers representing distances from two perpendicular axes was influenced by Indian trigonometric methods rather than earlier geometric constructions.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The introduction of negative numbers and zero by Brahmagupta represented a significant leap forward in the development of algebraic geometry, which Descartes would later build upon.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Brahmagupta's work on negative numbers provided a foundation for what Descartes used to define points in a two-dimensional plane using coordinates.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The use of coordinates as a tool for navigation and geometric problem solving by Omar Khayyam was not influenced by earlier Indian works but rather by European mathematicians after him.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Baudhāyana's work on the Baudhāyana–Pythagoras Theorem predates Descartes' formalisation of coordinates, and thus had no influence on Cartesian geometry.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The concept of a zero-centric coordinate plane was developed by Brahmagupta independently of earlier Indian works or any other influences.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Al-Bīrūnī's study of the Indian decimal system and algebraic formalism contributed to his ability to calculate coordinates across Asia, influencing later European mathematicians like Descartes.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The use of negative numbers in Brahmagupta’s work was a critical step towards creating the four-quadrant Cartesian plane that Descartes would develop further.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The Ujjayinī meridian's role as a zero-longitude reference for early Arabic maps indicates its influence from Indian mathematical works rather than purely Greek traditions.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In Quadrant I, both x- and y-coordinates are positive.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$A point on the y-axis has an x-coordinate of zero but can have any value for its y-coordinate.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The Cartesian plane divides the space into four quadrants with equal area each.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If a point P(x, y) lies in Quadrant IV, then both coordinates of P are negative.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$A point on the x-axis has a positive x-coordinate but can have any value for its y-coordinate.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The distance between two points (x1, y1) and (x2, y2) in 2-D space is always calculated using the formula √((x2 - x1)² + (y2 - y1)²).$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If a point Q(x, y) has coordinates that are negative integers, it must be in Quadrant III.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The origin O represents the only point where both x- and y-coordinates are zero.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For any two points (x1, y1) and (x2, y2), if x1 > x2 and y1 < y2, then the point with coordinates (x1, y1) is to the left of and above the other point.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If a point R has coordinates (5, -3) in Quadrant IV, it would be closer to the origin than point S with coordinates (-4, 2).$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$A point at (0, 6) is directly above the x-axis and below the y-axis.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Points P(-3, -5) and Q(1, 2) are in different quadrants based on their coordinates alone.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '8ece99ec-653f-496b-9fe5-0fb9700be044', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If two points have identical x-coordinates but different y-coordinates, they must lie in the same quadrant.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-714Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
